&Q000358 = How grain came to Sumer
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.1.7.6
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.1.7.6&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. uŋ₃-e udu-gin₇ u₂ ka-ba mu-ni-ib-<<ni>>-[gu₇]
#tr.en: Men used to eat grass with their mouths like sheep.
#lem: uŋ[people]; udu[sheep]; u[plant(s)]; kag[mouth]; gu[eat]
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. ud re-a {d}ezina₂ še gu nu-[zu]
#tr.en: In those times, they did not know grain, barley or flax.
#lem: ud[sun]; re[that]; Ezina[1]DN; še[barley]; gu[cord]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. an-ne₂ an-šag₄-ta im-da-an-ed₃-de₃
#tr.en: @wDN{An} brought these down from the interior of heaven.
#lem: An[1]DN; anšag[the interior of heaven]; ed[go up]
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. {d}en-lil₂-le a₂!(DA) tarah-gin₇ hur-saŋ galam X-da ed₃-de₃ igi mi-ni-ib-il₂-il₂-i
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil} lifted his gaze around as a stag lifts its horns when climbing the terraced …… hills.
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; a[arm]; durah[wild goat]; hursaŋ[mountain]; galam[skilful]; X; ed[go up]; igi[eye]; il[raise]
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. igi-ni sig-še₃ mu-un-il₂ a-ab-ba sug₄-ga-am₃
#tr.en: He looked southwards and saw the wide sea;
#lem: igi[eye]; sig[weak]; il[raise]; aʾabak[sea]; sug[full]
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. igi-nim-še₃ mu-un-il₂ kur šim {ŋiš}erin-na-kam
#tr.en: he looked northwards and saw the mountain of aromatic cedars.
#lem: iginim[upper land]; il[raise]; kur[mountain(s)]; šim[aromatic substance]; eren[cedar]
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. {d}en-lil₂-le še in-dub# kur-re ba-an-šum₂
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil} piled up the barley, gave it to the mountain.
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; še[barley]; dub[heap up]; kur[mountain(s)]; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. he₂-ŋal₂ kalam-ma-ke₄ in-X kur in-nu-ha# X im-ma#-an-šum₂#
#tr.en: He piled up the bounty of the Land, gave the @fsux{innuḫa} barley to the mountain.
#lem: heŋal[plenty]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; X; kur[mountain(s)]; in.nu.HA[type of barley]; X; šum[give]
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. hur-saŋ ŋal₂ da₁₃-da₁₃# igi ba-ni-in-tab-tab
#tr.en: He closed off access to the wide-open hill.
#lem: hursaŋ[mountain]; ŋal[open]; taka[set aside]; igi[eye]; tab[double]
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. {ŋiš}saŋ-kul-bi an# ki X [...]
#tr.en: He …… its lock,
#lem: saŋkul[bolt]; an[sky]; ki[place]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. {ŋiš}suhubₓ(|ŠU.EŠ.DI|)-bi [...] X [...]
#tr.en: which heaven and earth shut fast (?),
#lem: suhub[door bolt]; X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=11

12. AN [...] MA X GAR [...] im-mi-in-[...]
#tr.en: its bolt, which …….
#lem: X; X; X; X; X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. ud-ba {d}nin-a-zu X KA# [...]
#tr.en: Then @wDN{Ninazu} ……, and said to his brother @wDN{Ninmada}:
#lem: ud[sun]; Ninazu[1]DN; X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=13

14. šeš-a-ni {d}nin-ma-da-ra# gu₃# [mu-na-de₂-e]
#tr.en: @q[Ninazu,Ninmada]{“Let us go to the mountain,
#lem: šeš[brother]; Ninmadak[1]DN; gu[voice]; de[pour]
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. kur-še₃ ga-e-re₇-en-de₃-en# [...]
#tr.en: to the mountain where barley and flax grow;
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; ere[go (perfect plural stem of ŋen⟦to go⟧)]; X
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. kur še gu mu₂-mu₂ X [...]
#tr.en: …… the rolling river,
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; še[barley]; gu[cord]; mu[grow]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. id₂# hal-hal a ki-ta |DU.DU| X AM MA X X X
#tr.en: where the water wells up from the earth.
#lem: id[river]; hal[roll (around)]; a[water]; ki[place]; X; X; X; X; X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=17

#etcsl#doc on upper edge, possibly a continuation of the line:

18. [še kur-ba ga]-am₃-ta#-[ab-ed₃-en-de₃-en]
#tr.en: Let us fetch the barley down from its mountain,
#lem: še[barley]; kur[mountain(s)]; ed[go up]
#etcsl: line-id=18

19. in-[nu-ha ki]-en-gi X [...] X# [...]
#tr.en: let us introduce the @fsux{innuḫa} barley into @wGN{Sumer}.
#lem: in.nu.HA[type of barley]; Kengir[1]; X; X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=19

20. ki-en-gi še nu-zu še gi-bi₂-[...]
#tr.en: Let us make barley known in @wGN{Sumer}, which knows no barley.”}
#lem: Kengir[1]; še[barley]; zu[know]; še[barley]; X
#etcsl: line-id=20

21. {d}nin-ma-da šudu₃ an-na-ke₄ [mu-na-ni-ib-gi₄-gi₄]
#tr.en: @wDN{Ninmada}, the worshipper of @wDN{An}, replied to him:
#lem: Ninmadak[1]DN; šud[prayer]; An[1]DN; gi[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=21

22. niŋ₂ a-a-me nu-mu-un-dug₄-ga# [...]
#tr.en: @q[Ninmada,Ninazu]{“Since our father has not given the command,
#lem: niŋ[thing]; aya[father]; dug[speak]; X
#etcsl: line-id=22

23. niŋ₂ {d}en-lil₂-le nu-mu-un-dug₄-ga# [...]
#tr.en: since @wDN{Enlil} has not given the command,
#lem: niŋ[thing]; Enlil[1]DN; dug[speak]; X
#etcsl: line-id=23

24. a-na-gin₇-nam kur-še₃ i₃-sub₂-be₂-en-de₃#-[en]
#tr.en: how can we go there to the mountain?
#lem: anagin[how?]; kur[mountain(s)]; sub[imperfect plural stem of ŋen⟦to go⟧]
#etcsl: line-id=24

25. še kur-ba a-na#-gin₇-nam# im-ta-ab#-ed₃-de₃-en-de₃#-[en]
#tr.en: How can we bring down the barley from its mountain?
#lem: še[barley]; kur[mountain(s)]; anagin[how?]; ed[go up]
#etcsl: line-id=25

26. in-nu-ha ki-en#-gi a-na-gin₇-[nam] im-ma-ni-ib-kur₉-en-de₃-en
#tr.en: How can we introduce the @fsux{innuḫa} grain into @wGN{Sumer}?
#lem: in.nu.HA[type of barley]; Kengir[1]; anagin[how?]; kur[enter]
#etcsl: line-id=26

27. ki-en-gi še nu-zu a-na-gin₇#-nam im-bi₂-ib-zu-zu-un#-de₃-en#
#tr.en: How can we make barley known in @wGN{Sumer}, which knows no barley?”}
#lem: Kengir[1]; še[barley]; zu[know]; anagin[how?]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=27

28. ŋen-na {d}utu an-na ga-ba-ni-[re₇]-en-de₃-en#
#tr.en: @q{“Come, let us go to @wDN{Utu} of heaven, who as he lies there,
#lem: ŋen[go]; Utu[1]DN; an[sky]; ere[go (perfect plural stem of ŋen⟦to go⟧)]
#etcsl: line-id=28

29. lu₂ ba-nu₂-a lu₂ ba-nu₂-a u₃-sa₂# ku-ku#-nam
#tr.en: as he lies there, sleeps a sound sleep, to the hero,
#lem: lu[person]; nud[lie down]; lu[person]; nud[lie down]; usag[sleep]; ku[place]
#etcsl: line-id=29

30. ur-saŋ dumu {d}nin-gal lu₂ ba!-nu₂-a u₃-sa₂ ku-ku-nam
#tr.en: the son of @wDN{Ningal}, who as he lies there sleeps a sound sleep.”}
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; dumu[child]; Ningal[1]DN; lu[person]; nud[lie down]; usag[sleep]; ku[place]
#etcsl: line-id=30

31. {d}utu {ŋiš}ig 70-am₃ šu mu-na-an-zig₃
#tr.en: He raised his hands towards @wDN{Utu} of the seventy doors (?).
#lem: Utu[1]DN; ig[door]; n; šu[hand]; zig[rise]
#etcsl: line-id=31

32. {d}utu {ŋiš}banšur# AŠ KI
#tr.en: @wDN{Utu} …… table (?) …….
#lem: Utu[1]DN; banšur[table]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=32







